From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:48:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Precompute exact tail-division reciprocals and remove
 rank-one copies

Upstream base: f39c334c62f4fca1744c6563f40226ec0e9a71aa. Rationale: generic division on tiny tail copies prevented a proven improvement. Replace it with multiply-high plus one exact correction, and return the rank-one layout as a view. Quality: unsigned 32-bit division is exact across the full input range; no payload arithmetic. Tests: 10,070 independent integer-reference comparisons, broader opaque-payload matrix over five world sizes; GPU performance and two-boot tests pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
---
